# =========================================================
# Frontend environment variables.
#
# You usually do NOT need a .env file here for local development.
# During development, package.json has "proxy": "http://localhost:5000",
# which forwards anything starting with /api to the backend. That keeps the
# browser on one origin, so there is no CORS and no cross-site cookie issue.
#
# If you DO create a .env file here, remember:
#   - Only variables starting with REACT_APP_ are visible to the app.
#   - Everything here is BUNDLED INTO THE JAVASCRIPT and shipped to every
#     visitor's browser. It is not secret. Never put an API key, a password,
#     a database URL or a JWT secret in this file. Those belong in
#     server/.env, which is never sent to the browser.
# =========================================================

# The full address of your backend API, used only in production when the
# frontend and backend are hosted separately.
# Leave this unset for local development so the proxy above is used.
#
# Example: REACT_APP_API_URL=https://your-api-host.example.com/api
#
# If you set this, the backend must also allow your frontend's origin.
# Set CLIENT_ORIGIN in server/.env to the exact address of the frontend.
# REACT_APP_API_URL=
